  {
    "id": "3c8a64214e3c1dca4791d5f0",
    "path": "parquet_variant::builder::ParentState",
    "name": "ParentState",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "parquet-variant",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct ParentState<'a, S: BuilderSpecificState>",
    "docs": "Tracks information needed to correctly finalize a nested builder.\n\nA child builder has no effect on its parent unless/until its `finalize` method is called, at\nwhich point the child appends the new value to the parent. As a (desirable) side effect,\ncreating a parent state instance captures mutable references to a subset of the parent's fields,\nrendering the parent object completely unusable until the parent state goes out of scope. This\nensures that at most one child builder can exist at a time.\n\nThe redundancy in `value_builder` and `metadata_builder` is because all the references come from\nthe parent, and we cannot \"split\" a mutable reference across two objects (parent state and the\nchild builder that uses it). So everything has to be here.",
